📘 Real-Time Example in Code
Let’s see a simple Java code example for O(n) Time and Space Complexity:

java

import java.util.*;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 10, 15, 20, 25}; // Input array
        int sum = 0; // Constant space O(1)

        // O(n) time
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            sum += arr[i];  // adding each element
        }

        System.out.println("Sum of array: " + sum);
    }
}
Analysis:
Time Complexity:

Loop runs n times → O(n)

Space Complexity:

We use only 1 variable (sum) → O(1) (no extra space depending on n)

📘 How to Check Time and Space Complexity in a Program?
🔵 For Time Complexity:

Count how many times loops run.

Nested loops? Multiply (n * n = n²).

Function calls? Add or multiply their time.

Recursive calls? Solve recurrence (e.g., divide by 2 each time → O(log n)).

🔵 For Space Complexity:

Look at extra variables (arrays, hashmaps, recursion stack).

Space proportional to n? → O(n)

Constant extra space? → O(1)

📘 Step-by-Step Checking Guide
Step	Question to Ask	Example
1	How many loops?	One loop → O(n)
2	Any nested loops?	Two nested loops → O(n²)
3	Recursion?	Calls itself? → analyze call depth
4	Extra memory used?	Creating new array? O(n) space

📘 Visual Feeling (Shortcut)
Code Structure	Time Complexity
Single loop	O(n)
Two nested loops	O(n²)
Dividing by 2 each time (binary search)	O(log n)
Recursion for all subsets	O(2^n)
Simple addition/subtraction/multiplication	O(1)

📘 Final Short Definitions
✅ Time Complexity:
"How much time your code takes to run depending on input size."

✅ Space Complexity:
"How much extra memory your code needs during execution depending on input size."

✅ Big O:
"A standard way to express time/space complexity (ignoring constants)."

